Description: ui/gtk: Copy the views of a stereo scanout at their own resolution
 .
 The subsurface held both views scaled to the size one view is shown
 at, so a top-and-bottom or side by side (half) scanout was stretched
 back to full size here and resized again by the compositor to the
 window.
 .
 Copy each view as the guest scans it out instead: a top-and-bottom
 1920x1080 frame becomes one 3840x540 buffer, a side by side (half)
 frame two 960x1080 views.  The viewport, which already has the size
 a view is shown at, gives the compositor the one resize.
Author: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Origin: https://github.com/Sparky-OS/qemu/commit/5a5010982b3012fdd1af5b8160c21f858ad8f0d3
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-10-22
Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
